__pycache__/
*.pyc
.pytest_cache/
*.egg-info/

# Per-cycle snapshot-driven pipeline scratch files (bot/README.md "Snapshot-driven mode").
# Contain live account data (cash, positions, cost basis, tax lots) and/or an unapproved
# trade plan awaiting user confirmation — never committed; only the specific files listed
# in a plan/finalize result's `files_changed` are committed each cycle.
/snapshot.json
/plan_result*.json
/finalize_result.json
/price_fetch_plan.json
/fetched_bars.json
/price_cache_result.json

# Ad-hoc scratch files (report tables, PnL matching, email body assembly, etc.) built by
# the agent while composing the Step 9 email report each cycle — same rationale as above:
# live account data, never committed.
/scratch_*
/email_body.html
/email_body_plain.md

# Stateful data files (v2.86.0) — live on Google Drive only (bot/drive_sync.py), pulled at the
# start of every cycle and pushed at the end. Never git-tracked: the container that runs a cycle
# is ephemeral, so git-tracking these would either go stale between cycles or (as before) commit
# live account data to a public paper trail unnecessarily. logs/trade_journal.md is NOT here — it
# stays git-tracked (the actual paper trail) AND is separately mirrored to Drive.
/peak/prices.json
/tax/realized_gains_by_year.json
/price_history/daily_bars.json
/logs/history_trade_journal-*.md
